.TH TRAIL-FRONTMATTER 5 2026-10-17 "Peios trail 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
trail-frontmatter \- Trail article metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
<article>.md
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every article begins with a YAML frontmatter block: a line of exactly
\fB---\fR,
the keys, and a closing \fB---\fR. It must be the first thing in the file.
\fBUnknown keys are build errors.\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
---
title: Command-line reference
type: reference
description: Every pekit flag with its value form, the capability matrix, and exit codes.
related:
  - pekit/running/invocation
  - pekit/reference/recipe-format
inline_ref:
  - pekit CLI
updated: 2026-05-01
reading_minutes: 25
---
.fi
.PP
.SS "The keys"
.PP
.TP
\fBtitle\fR
Type: string; Topic article: \fBrequired\fR; Book article: \fBrequired\fR
.TP
\fBtype\fR
Type: string; Topic article: \fBrequired\fR; Book article: \fBerror\fR
.TP
\fBdescription\fR
Type: string; Topic article: optional; Book article: optional
.TP
\fBrelated\fR
Type: array of strings; Topic article: optional; Book article: optional
.TP
\fBinline_ref\fR
Type: array of strings; Topic article: optional; Book article: optional
.TP
\fBupdated\fR
Type: ISO date; Topic article: optional; Book article: optional
.TP
\fBreading_minutes\fR
Type: integer; Topic article: optional; Book article: optional
.PP
.SS "The title field"
.PP
The page's name: its \fBh1\fR, breadcrumb, sidebar entry, search-result
heading
and \fBog:title\fR. Never derived  -  an article always states its own.
.PP
.SS "The type field"
.PP
The learn taxonomy. Required on articles in topics; **an error on articles in
books**, where the question it answers is already settled by the document's
order.
.PP
Trail does not constrain the value and does not display it on the page. It is
carried into \fBsite.json\fR as the article's \fBtype\fR. This site uses
\fBconcept\fR,
\fBhow-to\fR, and \fBreference\fR.
.PP
.SS "The description field"
.PP
One sentence. It feeds:
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fB<meta name="description">\fR and \fBog:description\fR;
.IP \(bu 2
the standfirst line of the page's
  markdown mirror;
.IP \(bu 2
the \fBdescription\fR field in \fBsite.json\fR.
.PP
It is not shown on the page, and it is not the in-site search snippet  -
Pagefind builds those from body text.
.PP
\fB--strict\fR fails the build on any article without one.
Alias pages are exempt.
.PP
.SS "The related field"
.PP
Page references in the \fB~\fR grammar,
\fBwithout the leading \fB~\fR\fR:
.PP
.PP
.nf
related:
  - pekit/running/invocation
  - peios/package-management/overview
.fi
.PP
They render as a "Related Content" list under the article, appear in the
markdown mirror, and become a list of resolved paths in \fBsite.json\fR.
.PP
Resolution is as strict as a body link: **ambiguous references always fail the
build**; missing ones fail unless \fB--allow-dangling-links\fR downgrades them
to
a warning, in which case they are dropped from the list.
.PP
.SS "inline_ref"
.PP
Phrases that should link to this article wherever they appear in the site's
prose:
.PP
.PP
.nf
inline_ref:
  - PCDS GUID
  - PCDS GUIDs
.fi
.PP
Matching is literal, whole-word and longest-first, and skips headings, links,
image alt text, code, and the claiming page itself. A phrase belongs to
exactly one declarer site-wide; a collision is a build error, as is an empty
phrase, one with leading or trailing whitespace, or one containing \fBsection
\fR. Alias
pages claim nothing. See
Inline references.
.PP
.SS "The updated field"
.PP
An ISO \fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR date, validated as such:
.PP
.PP
.nf
updated: '2026/05/01' is not an ISO date (expected YYYY-MM-DD)
.fi
.PP
It appears in the page's meta line and becomes the page's \fB<lastmod>\fR in
\fBsitemap.xml\fR. Containers take the most recent date beneath them.
.PP
Deliberately manual: file modification times are noise, and trail does not
read git history.
.PP
.PP
never \fB2026-5-1\fR. No quoting is needed  -  an unquoted date works.
.PP
.SS "reading_minutes"
.PP
An integer overriding the estimate, which is otherwise the body's word count
at 200 words a minute, rounded up, with a floor of 1. Code blocks count toward
the word count.
.PP
Containers sum their children's values, so a book cover reports the whole
book.
.PP
.SS "Errors"
.PP
.TP
\fB... has no frontmatter (must start with '---')\fR
Cause: The file does not open with \fB---\fR.
.TP
\fB... has unterminated frontmatter\fR
Cause: No closing \fB---\fR.
.TP
\fBparsing frontmatter of ...\fR
Cause: Invalid YAML, a missing required key, or an unknown key.
.TP
\fBupdated: '...' is not an ISO date (expected YYYY-MM-DD)\fR
Cause: A malformed date.
.PP
Inside a book, \fBtype:\fR produces an unknown-key error, since \fBtype\fR is
not part
of the book article schema.
.PP
.SS "Frontmatter and .link aliases"
.PP
An alias page has no frontmatter of
its own  -  it renders the target's body. It takes its title from the
\fB.link\fR
file (or from its own slug), its canonical URL from the original, and it
claims no \fBinline_ref\fR phrases. Inside a book it also loses \fBtype\fR and
\fBdescription\fR, as every book entry does.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trail (1),
.BR trail.toml (5)
.PP
